# The virtualenv lives outside the repo on purpose (see README.md §4):
#   /workspace/venvs/baseline
# Only sources, scripts and evidence belong in this directory.
# NOTE: the evidence files themselves are NEVER listed here -- they are deliverables, and a
# missing one must show up as a diff instead of being hidden by an ignore rule.
venv/
*.whl
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Temp / backup / editor leftovers.
# The evidence collectors write "<name>.tmp" next to the target and only move it into place
# when the run completed (temp+sentinel), so a failed or interrupted run legitimately leaves
# a *.tmp behind: it must never be committed. A stray evidence/.02-version-matrix.tmp did get
# committed once (caught by the r4 merge gate); these rules are what stop it from happening
# again. Both forms are listed: "*.tmp" for plain names and ".*.tmp" for the dot-prefixed
# temp the collectors actually produce.
*.tmp
.*.tmp
*.temp
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.nfs*
